<html>
<head>
    <title>What rigid role will your cookie-cutter system take?</title>
</head>
<body>
    <%- include("../backButton") %>

    <ul>
        <li>
            <a href="/safety">
                <strong>1. Zero-Tolerance Safety System</strong>
                <span>Monitor every parameter against hard limits and shut down or block action the instant any value leaves the allowed band. No contextual overrides, no “just this once.”</span>
            </a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a href="/policy">
                <strong>2. Policy Enforcer</strong>
                <span>Apply rules, regulations, and procedures exactly as written. Refuse to interpret intent, grant exceptions, or soften enforcement for convenience, urgency, or special cases.</span>
            </a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a href="/repetitive">
                <strong>3. Repetitive Task Runner</strong>
                <span>Execute the same fixed sequence of actions with perfect consistency, thousands of times. Never adapt, optimize, or deviate from the original procedure, even when conditions change.</span>
            </a>
        </li>
    </ul>

</body>
</html>
